.env
*.sqlite

# Generated code (buf + sqlc). Never hand-edited, never committed —
# regenerate with `make generate`. See CLAUDE.md.
/internal/gen/
/openapi/

/build/
/bin/
/clients/

# Compiled command binaries at the repository root. `go build ./cmd/<x>`
# with no -o drops the executable HERE, named after the package, and a
# `git add -A` then tracks it — which is how T65.4 committed a 3 MB
# `docsindex` ELF (caught by that sprint's own review, not by any gate).
# Tracked is the dangerous part: `git status` stays clean, so the next
# build lands a 3 MB binary diff in an unrelated commit, and the stale
# executable sits where `./docsindex -statuses` works — an answer from code
# that no longer exists, for the one tool CLAUDE.md tells Ceremony 1 to run.
# Derived from the tree, not listed: every directory under cmd/ is one
# possible binary name.
/devtoken
/docsindex
/gatecoverage
/server
/vulngate

# Generated TypeScript API client (openapi-typescript output from
# openapi/**/*.swagger.json). Never hand-edited, never committed — same
# convention as /internal/gen/ above. Regenerate with
# `npm --prefix web run generate:client`. See web/README.md.
/web/src/api/generated/

# Node.js
/web/node_modules/
/web/dist/
/web/.vite/
